@startuml
!define REGISTER_WIDTH 32

skinparam rectangle {
    BackgroundColor<<register>> LightGray
    BorderColor Black
}

rectangle "SDMA System Address / Argument 2 Register (Offset 000h)" <<register>> {
    rectangle "D31" as D31
    rectangle "..." as middle
    rectangle "D00" as D00
}

D31 -right-> middle
middle -right-> D00

note bottom of D31
  **Bits 31-00: SDMA System Address / Argument 2 (RW)**
  
  (1) **SDMA System Address**
  - Contains physical system memory address for DMA transfers
  - Points to next contiguous data position when transfer stops
  - Can only be accessed when no transaction is executing
  - Initialized by Host Driver before starting SDMA transaction
  - Transfer waits at boundaries specified by Host SDMA Buffer Boundary
  - Host Controller generates DMA Interrupt to request updates
  - Writing to 003h restarts SDMA transfer
  - When restarting via Resume command or Continue Request,
    starts at address stored here
  - ADMA does not use this register
  
  (2) **Argument 2**
  - Used with Auto CMD23 to set 32-bit block count value
  - With ADMA: full 32-bit block count value can be used
  - Without ADMA: limited by Block Count register (max 65535 blocks)
end note

@enduml